From: canoziia <canoziia@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] kv cache: let DFlash drafter layers ride the GLM5Next MLA tensors

KV init failed for every block size once a DFlash/DFlash2 drafter was
attached: its sliding-window layers sent grouping to the generic page
unifier, which cannot fit the kpool indexer page. Place the drafter layers
on the MLA tensors at disjoint block ids, 1024 tokens per drafter block in
one MLA page (the rest of the page is padding; 4 of 5 MiB at target block
5120). 1024 divides the drafter's 2048-token window and the 5120-token
target block/LMCache chunk, so the geometry needs no LMCache change. Padded
pages are never split into smaller kernel blocks.

The scheduler aligned Mamba (KDA) state checkpoints to the smallest group
block, i.e. the drafter's 1024, instead of the target state page; local
prefill and an LMCache restore could then snapshot the KDA state at
different positions. Checkpoints now follow the homogeneous
MambaSpec.block_size; mixed Mamba block sizes keep the old behaviour.
At target block 5120, --max-num-batched-tokens must be 5184 so a full block
still fits next to the draft input slots.

Grouping without a drafter is unchanged.

diff --git a/vllm/v1/core/kv_cache_utils.py b/vllm/v1/core/kv_cache_utils.py
--- a/vllm/v1/core/kv_cache_utils.py
+++ b/vllm/v1/core/kv_cache_utils.py
@@ -1181,10 +1181,23 @@
         for name, spec in kv_cache_spec.items()
         if isinstance(spec, KpoolTailSpec)
     }
+    # A spec-decode drafter that carries its own attention (DFlash/DFlash2)
+    # registers plain sliding-window layers on top of the GLM-5.3-Flash
+    # hybrid. Partition them out -- exact type, since KpoolTailSpec subclasses
+    # SlidingWindowSpec -- so they do not disqualify the model from this
+    # layout; they become extra groups below (_glm5_next_draft_groups).
+    # Without such a drafter draft_specs is empty and nothing below changes.
+    # Ported from Morrowmake/vllm-cmp170hx v1/core/kv_cache_utils.py.
+    draft_specs = {
+        name: spec
+        for name, spec in kv_cache_spec.items()
+        if type(spec) is SlidingWindowSpec
+    }
     attn_specs = {
         name: spec
         for name, spec in kv_cache_spec.items()
         if not isinstance(spec, (MambaSpec, KpoolTailSpec))
+        and type(spec) is not SlidingWindowSpec
     }
     if not mamba_specs or not all(
         type(spec) is MLAAttentionSpec for spec in attn_specs.values()
@@ -1241,11 +1254,129 @@
     for index, name in enumerate(mamba_specs):
         mamba_grouped_names[index % num_groups].append(name)
 
+    draft_groups: list[KVCacheGroupSpec] = []
+    if draft_specs:
+        draft_groups = _glm5_next_draft_groups(
+            vllm_config, draft_specs, mla_specs, mla_names, mla_page
+        )
+        if not draft_groups:
+            # Unsupported drafter geometry: fall back to the generic path
+            # (which cannot unify the kpool indexer page and will raise).
+            # _glm5_next_draft_groups has logged why.
+            return None
+        spec_config = vllm_config.speculative_config
+        if spec_config is not None and spec_config.use_eagle_block_drop():
+            for draft_group in draft_groups:
+                draft_group.is_eagle_group = True
